// meta_sysml_risk.hymeko — risk assessment and decision-option vocabulary.
//
// Extends meta_sysml_structure.hymeko (not modified) with what a risk register in the style of
// NIST SP 800-30 Rev. 1, an Ishikawa (cause–effect) view and a decision view need.
// Plan: docs/plans/2026-10-07-risk-decision.
//
// Element kinds (the consumer chooses the fields; the views read the ones named here):
//   hazard         an undesired top outcome; the head of an Ishikawa diagram
//   risk           a scenario: category -> risk_category; likelihood_initial, impact_initial (before)
//                  and likelihood_residual, impact_residual (after the mitigating requirements)
//                  -> scale levels; the level itself is never stored, it is read from the cells
//   risk_category  an Ishikawa bone
//   risk_cell      one cell of a likelihood × impact table: likelihood -> , impact -> , level ->
//   decision       an open or decided design question
//   option         one answer to a decision; its effects are the edges below
// Scale: a consumer declares its levels `<isa> scale_level` with a numeric `rank` (1 = lowest).
//
// Sign conventions (+ / - / ~ are incidence roles, not weights):
//   mitigates  (+ requirement..., - risk)            requirements whose satisfaction gives the residual values
//   leads_to   (+ risk, - risk | hazard)             cause → effect; chains form the Ishikawa ribs
//   considers  (+ decision, - option...)
//   selects    (+ option, - product_candidate)       the candidate replaces the line it is alternative_of
//   adds       (+ option, - product_candidate, ~ block)  the candidate is procured and realizes the block
//   omits      (+ option, - product)                 the line is not procured
//   overrides  (+ option, - constraint)              edge fields value / value_max replace the
//                                                    constraint's; field basis states the assumption
//   introduces (+ option, - constraint)              the constraint is checked only in this option

meta_sysml_risk {
    // Both imported directly: a `using` of a transitively imported module does not resolve once
    // this file is itself imported (Core observation, reports/2026-10-07-derived-trace.md).
    @"../paper/meta_sysml_trace.hymeko";
    @"meta_sysml_structure.hymeko";
    using meta_sysml_trace.sysml_trace as tr;
    using meta_sysml_structure.sysml_structure as st;
}

sysml_risk {
    elements {
        hazard:        + <isa> tr.elements.meta_element {}
        risk:          + <isa> tr.elements.meta_element {}
        risk_category: + <isa> tr.elements.meta_element {}
        risk_cell:     + <isa> tr.elements.meta_element {}
        decision:      + <isa> tr.elements.meta_element {}
        option:        + <isa> tr.elements.meta_element {}
    }

    scales {
        scale_level {}
    }

    @mitigates {}
    @leads_to {}
    @considers {}
    @selects {}
    @adds {}
    @omits {}
    @overrides {}
    @introduces {}
}
